  "notes": "{伏|ふ}せる has two main meanings: to turn something face down (physical), and to hide or conceal information.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: Xを{伏|ふ}せる (to turn X face down / to conceal X)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{伏|ふ}せている means \"is face down\" or \"is being kept hidden\" (resulting state).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- カードを{伏|ふ}せる: turn a card face down\n- コップを{伏|ふ}せる: turn a cup upside down\n- {目|め}を{伏|ふ}せる: cast one's eyes down\n- {名前|なまえ}を{伏|ふ}せる: withhold a name\n- {事実|じじつ}を{伏|ふ}せる: conceal a fact\n\nUSAGE:\nSense 1 (face down) appears in instructions and descriptions. Sense 2 (concealing) is common in news and formal writing, especially when sources or names are withheld.",
